UID:122650-1785072600-1785076200@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Rooted in Time: Living Fossils
DESCRIPTION:Join us and the North Carolina Fossil Club for a special presentation in the SECU Daily Planet Theater with paleontologist Dr. Carole Gee! \nWhat are living fossils? How can we sort out living plant and animal species from their lookalikes in the fossil record? Should living fossils be considered primitive forms or viewed instead as unique examples of our evolutionary heritage? Find out more at this public meeting of the NC Fossil Club! This program is free and registration is not required. Seating in the SECU Daily Planet Theater is limited. \nDr. Carole Gee is a paleontologist who specializes in Mesozoic and Cenozoic plants. After graduating with a Ph.D. in Botany from the University of Texas at Austin\, during which she spent a year in Sweden as a Fulbright scholar\, Carole first moved on to ETH Zurich in Switzerland for a postdoc to study fossil pollen and spores\, then to Bonn in Germany to return to fossil plant research on the organismal level. Dr. Gee was a paleobotanist\, botanist\, and professor of paleontology at the University of Bonn from 1990 until her recent retirement in January 2026. \nThis presentation is a collaboration with the NC Fossil Club.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/rooted-in-time-living-fossils/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:General Events,Lectures,Meet the Scientist,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Smith":MAILTO:christopher.smith@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822405;-78.6409677
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Nature Research Center 121 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=121 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6409677,35.7822405
END:VEVENT
